{%- import "lib.j2" as lib -%}
{#-
  Qyl.SpanNames: one method per span row that registry/qyl/policy.yaml gives a `qyl.span_name`
  chain of its own. The chain is a list of templates; the first whose every {key} placeholder has
  a non-empty value names the span, after the row's substitutions rewrote a value (null: treat it
  as absent). The starters and qyl's interceptors call the same methods, so both produce the same
  names. A placeholder key the row does not list as an attribute (db.system.name on db.sql.client,
  rpc.system.name on the gRPC rows) is still a string parameter: the rule needs it. Every rule
  ships in the stable package, whatever the span's tier: the producer packages
  may not read the incubating tier, and a naming rule names no vocabulary.
-#}
